description:
Most code is _synchronous_, which means it runs all in line, one by one, like this:
```ts
console.log("I print first");
console.log("I print second");
console.log("I print third");
```
Asynchronous code (AKA `async`) runs `concurrently`. While the main process runs code, `async` processes are handled separately whenever possible allowed by the system resources. A good demonstration for this is [setTimeout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/setTimeout). `setTimeout` takes two arguments: a callback, and the amount of milliseconds until the callback should run, EG:
```ts
console.log("I print first");
setTimeout(
    (): void => { console.log("I print last because I wait"); },
    123
);
console.log("I print second");
```

---
## Assignment: To demonstrate how `async` code works, let's practice. (Note that you will never do somthing like this in real code). Update the durations at the start so it prints in the order
1. Opening MeTube
2. Connecting to Server USANE
3. Fetching for-you page
4. Opening video
5. Generating 120 seconds of unskippable adds
6. Fetched metadata. Title: \"How to write 'Hello, World!' in Brain***k, Befunge 98, and Malbolge.\" Length: 1:25:09"

starterCode:
const startupTime: number = 5;
const fetchAdsTime: number = 10;
const fetchForYouTime: number = 20;
const videoOpenTime: number = 50;
const metadataFetchTime: number = 100;
// Don't touch below this line
setTimeout(
  (): void => console.log("Connecting to Server USANE"),
  startupTime
);
setTimeout(
  (): void => console.log("Generating 120 seconds of unskippable adds"),
  fetchAdsTime
);
setTimeout(
  (): void => console.log("Fetching for-you page"),
  fetchForYouTime
);
setTimeout(
  (): void => console.log("Opening video"),
  videoOpenTime
);
setTimeout(
  (): void => console.log("Fetched metadata. Title: \"How to write 'Hello, World!' in Brain***k, Befunge 98, and Malbolge.\", Length: 1:25:09"),
  metadataFetchTime
);
console.log("Opening MeTube");

await sleep(2000);
function sleep(ms: number): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise<void>((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
}
